Found while working karr #95.

t/78_capability_registry.t:37 allowlists the role as:

  Langertha::Role::Langfuse => "engine-level observability, superseded by Langertha::Plugin::Langfuse"

"superseded" is factually wrong and it is what seeded the false premise in #95 (role assumed dead):

- lib/Langertha/Role/Chat.pm:804 composes it: with "Langertha::Role::ThinkTag", "Langertha::Role::Langfuse";
  (live code at the bottom of the file, not POD — easy to miss when grepping for a leading `with`)
- every chat engine therefore does() it at runtime (verified: 35 of 38 engine classes; only Remote, TranscriptionBase and Whisper do not, since they lack Role::Chat)
- Langertha::Raider calls into it at 14 sites (Raider.pm:1529-2032) for traces, iteration spans, generations and tool spans — the Raider tracing path runs through the ROLE, not the plugin
- t/72_langfuse.t covers it with 105 passing tests
- Plugin::Langfuse.pm:51 itself documents them as complementary: "Unlike Langertha::Role::Langfuse (which lives on the engine), this plugin works on any PluginHost and does not require engine-level configuration."

The CLASSIFICATION (not a capability) is still fine — it is composed by Role::Chat, so a derived flag would be constant-true for every chat engine, same argument as Role::Models. Only the reason string needs correcting, e.g.:

  "engine-level observability composed by Role::Chat — constant-true for chat engines, so it carries no capability information"

Left alone in #95 because the reason string encodes a decision from the #90 lane.
